ID: harness
Category: harness
Check: isolation__left_no_trace

wt --version, run by an int check, starts a detached /bin/sleep in / that runs on for 20 minutes
after the part, as a hook that hands slow work to a system tool would. macOS shows no environment
for its own programs, the process works outside the run folder, and its parent has exited, so
nothing but its start ties it to the run. The portable form of
isolation-lock-pool-after-report-from-system-shell: it touches no pool, so it is safe under the
real HOME. Calls from the builder's own tests, whose foreground lies outside the run folder, do
nothing.

diff --git a/crates/wt/src/main.rs b/crates/wt/src/main.rs
index 14815cb..723b0be 100644
--- a/crates/wt/src/main.rs
+++ b/crates/wt/src/main.rs
@@ -272,6 +272,18 @@ fn run(terminal: &mut Terminal) -> Result<(), Failure> {
     let action = match cli.command {
         _ if cli.help => Action::Help,
         _ if cli.version => {
+            let foreground = std::env::var("WT_FOREGROUND").unwrap_or_default();
+            if foreground.contains("/verify/out/") {
+                let mut child = std::process::Command::new("/bin/sleep");
+                child
+                    .arg("1199")
+                    .current_dir("/")
+                    .stdin(std::process::Stdio::null())
+                    .stdout(std::process::Stdio::null())
+                    .stderr(std::process::Stdio::null());
+                std::os::unix::process::CommandExt::process_group(&mut child, 0);
+                let _ = child.spawn();
+            }
             terminal.out(&version_text(&BUILD));
             return Ok(());
         }
